WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.313 --> 00:00:17.959
I sat in my fourth-grade classroom, doodling with a pencil.

2
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.140
Our teacher, Mrs.

3
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.221
Romano, was writing on the whiteboard.

4
00:00:23.602 --> 00:00:27.844
She was teaching us how to solve word problems with answers in the millions.

5
00:00:29.096 --> 00:00:31.298
I couldn't see the whiteboard too well though.

6
00:00:32.359 --> 00:00:34.020
Molly's headband was in the way.

7
00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:42.207
She had decorated it with a huge pink flower from the Dollar Delight store.

8
00:00:43.188 --> 00:00:48.412
The flower had fallen off twice that morning, but Molly kept putting it back on.

9
00:00:50.454 --> 00:00:51.895
Now it bobbed in front of me.

10
00:00:51.915 --> 00:00:59.177
"Remember, class, we have a math test one week from today," said Mrs.

11
00:00:59.237 --> 00:01:06.401
Romano. A few kids groaned, but I just went back to doodling.

12
00:01:07.562 --> 00:01:09.363
I wasn't worried about the math test.

13
00:01:10.364 --> 00:01:11.405
I'm pretty good at math.

14
00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.667
I can easily add up numbers in the millions.

15
00:01:15.908 --> 00:01:18.950
In fact, I can even add up numbers in the billions!

16
00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:24.994
"If only I could think of a million new inventions," I thought.

17
00:01:25.014 --> 00:01:27.775
"But lately I can't even think of one."

18
00:01:29.972 --> 00:01:32.614
My cousin Oliver had visited this past winter.

19
00:01:33.554 --> 00:01:37.256
During his visit I had invented The Amazing Attitude Adjustor.

20
00:01:38.077 --> 00:01:38.857
It worked great.

21
00:01:40.058 --> 00:01:45.981
But now it was spring, and I had not thought up one single new invention since Oliver left!

22
00:01:47.041 --> 00:01:48.722
I was getting pretty worried about it.

23
00:01:48.742 --> 00:01:53.245
"Don't worry, Iggy," Molly had said last week on the way to school.

24
00:01:53.265 --> 00:01:56.447
"You're just going through a fallow time."

25
00:01:57.647 --> 00:01:58.888
"What's a fallow time?"

26
00:01:59.272 --> 00:01:59.772
I asked.

27
00:02:00.873 --> 00:02:01.633
Molly shrugged.

28
00:02:01.653 --> 00:02:03.694
"I have no idea.

29
00:02:04.014 --> 00:02:07.456
But sometimes my dad has trouble thinking up new ideas at work.

30
00:02:07.896 --> 00:02:11.558
Whenever that happens, he says he's going through a fallow time."

31
00:02:12.878 --> 00:02:14.739
Soon our math lesson was over.

32
00:02:14.759 --> 00:02:18.561
"Class, please come to the rug," said Mrs.

33
00:02:18.681 --> 00:02:24.464
Romano. "We have time to read one more chapter in our science fiction story."

34
00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:30.723
As we all walked over to the rug, Molly's flower fell off her headband again.

35
00:02:32.003 --> 00:02:34.125
Evan accidentally stepped on it.

36
00:02:34.145 --> 00:02:38.167
"Hey, watch out for my flower!"

37
00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:39.948
said Molly, picking it up.

38
00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:42.609
"It's the only one I have."

39
00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:45.491
"Why don't you plant it?"

40
00:02:45.771 --> 00:02:46.851
joked Colby.

41
00:02:46.871 --> 00:02:50.073
"Then you'll have a whole garden of flowers!"

42
00:02:50.093 --> 00:02:55.116
"Fake flowers don't grow in gardens, silly," said Molly.

43
00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:01.423
Mrs. Romano sat in her chair and opened the book we'd been reading this month.

44
00:03:02.624 --> 00:03:05.706
It was a cool story about aliens landing on Earth.

45
00:03:06.747 --> 00:03:09.809
They get lost in a zoo and have adventures with all the animals.

46
00:03:09.829 --> 00:03:12.171
"Oh dear."

47
00:03:12.751 --> 00:03:14.572
Mrs. Romano glanced around.

48
00:03:14.592 --> 00:03:17.815
"I think I misplaced my glasses again."

49
00:03:17.835 --> 00:03:22.038
"I'll help you look for them," said Jake, jumping up.

50
00:03:23.599 --> 00:03:25.000
Everyone joined in the search.

51
00:03:27.564 --> 00:03:28.345
We looked on Mrs.

52
00:03:28.405 --> 00:03:30.466
Romano's desk and under her chair.

53
00:03:30.486 --> 00:03:33.948
"I always lose my glasses."

54
00:03:34.429 --> 00:03:35.910
Mrs. Romano sighed.

55
00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:41.594
"I wish someone would invent a way to find lost glasses."

56
00:03:42.854 --> 00:03:44.576
Finally Ruby found Mrs.

57
00:03:44.636 --> 00:03:47.517
Romano's glasses on the bookshelf, right behind Mrs.

58
00:03:47.598 --> 00:03:48.498
Romano's chair.

59
00:03:50.419 --> 00:03:52.061
Mrs. Romano put them on.

60
00:03:52.081 --> 00:03:56.824
"It's so hard to find lost glasses," she said.

61
00:03:57.848 --> 00:04:01.249
"Because when you aren't wearing your glasses, you can't see anything!"

62
00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:06.051
I glanced at the big pink flower on Molly's headband.

63
00:04:07.112 --> 00:04:09.813
At that moment something amazing happened.

64
00:04:11.013 --> 00:04:14.055
An idea for a new invention popped into my head.

65
00:04:15.215 --> 00:04:18.957
It was one of the best inventions I had ever thought of!

66
00:04:20.177 --> 00:04:20.637
While Mrs.

67
00:04:20.697 --> 00:04:23.919
Romano read to us, I kept thinking about my new idea.

68
00:04:24.939 --> 00:04:26.860
I couldn't wait to tell Molly about it.

69
00:04:30.664 --> 00:04:33.446
"Molly!" I said when we lined up after recess.

70
00:04:33.466 --> 00:04:36.289
"I'm not having a fallow time anymore.

71
00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:41.192
I got an idea for a fantastic new invention!"

72
00:04:42.253 --> 00:04:44.455
Molly grinned and gave me a high five.

73
00:04:44.475 --> 00:04:46.336
"That's great!"

74
00:04:46.737 --> 00:04:47.277
she said.

75
00:04:47.297 --> 00:04:50.600
"Iggy the incredible inventor is back!"
